02:15:16,580 --> 02:15:17,620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is it 15 years?

2200
02:15:17,840 --> 02:15:19,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It was placed on record?

2201
02:15:20,640 --> 02:15:23,460
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: That was the record of several years ago, Po.

2202
02:15:23,460 --> 02:15:31,260
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: So, admittedly, it was maybe 15 years ago, the shelf life was 20 years.

2203
02:15:31,380 --> 02:15:33,540
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: And then it was reduced to 15.

2204
02:15:33,920 --> 02:15:39,300
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Now, the shelf life of a case was averaging nine years.

2205
02:15:40,860 --> 02:15:41,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Still a bit long.

2206
02:15:41,940 --> 02:15:43,020
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: A bit low, Po.

2207
02:15:43,040 --> 02:15:47,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Higher than the national average of cases in the first-level court.

2208
02:15:47,800 --> 02:15:48,240
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Yes, Po.

2209
02:15:48,240 --> 02:15:53,240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, something that the Sandigan Bayan will have to also,

2210
02:15:53,460 --> 02:15:54,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: work on, in terms of...

2211
02:15:54,920 --> 02:15:55,060
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Yes, Po.

2212
02:15:55,260 --> 02:16:01,640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But you were saying earlier, as of 2026, November, October, September,

2213
02:16:02,720 --> 02:16:05,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: the conviction rate is 82%.

2214
02:16:05,040 --> 02:16:05,620
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Yes, Po.

2215
02:16:05,840 --> 02:16:09,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, of the 535 cases...

2216
02:16:09,340 --> 02:16:09,640
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Pending.

2217
02:16:10,180 --> 02:16:10,580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pending.

2218
02:16:11,080 --> 02:16:16,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So far, the conviction has been pegged at 82%.

2219
02:16:16,740 --> 02:16:20,400
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Let me just clarify, Po.

2220
02:16:20,460 --> 02:16:20,780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, please.

2221
02:16:20,780 --> 02:16:22,780
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: The conviction is of the cases that were...

2222
02:16:23,460 --> 02:16:24,160
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Disposed.

2223
02:16:25,000 --> 02:16:28,380
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: So, in other words, of this year,

2224
02:16:29,960 --> 02:16:34,640
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: we disposed already...

2225
02:16:34,640 --> 02:16:39,620
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: 356 cases.

2226
02:16:39,620 --> 02:16:47,960
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Of the 356, 82% of those had convictions.

2227
02:16:48,260 --> 02:16:48,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

2228
02:16:48,760 --> 02:16:52,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because from 805 cases in 2025,

2229
02:16:52,160 --> 02:16:56,520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: you've dropped to 535 cases in 2026.

2230
02:16:56,620 --> 02:16:57,000
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Yes, Po.

2231
02:16:57,000 --> 02:17:00,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You disposed of about 300-plus cases.

2232
02:17:00,440 --> 02:17:02,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 330 cases.

2233
02:17:02,780 --> 02:17:07,640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And of the 330 cases, 82% is conviction.

2234
02:17:07,900 --> 02:17:08,400
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Yes, Po.

2235
02:17:08,540 --> 02:17:08,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

2236
02:17:09,560 --> 02:17:17,560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Did the flood control scandal have anything to do with your higher conviction rates?

2237
02:17:18,820 --> 02:17:20,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Of course, you cannot...

2238
02:17:20,160 --> 02:17:21,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You can only speculate.

2239
02:17:22,160 --> 02:17:31,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But it might be possible that it became a wake-up call for all of us, I hope.

2240
02:17:31,540 --> 02:17:32,960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If so, then that's good.

2241
02:17:34,020 --> 02:17:40,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's one silver lining in coming out of that scandal.

2242
02:17:41,220 --> 02:17:43,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Assuming, you know, maybe.

2243
02:17:43,780 --> 02:17:46,080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At least for us in the Senate,

2244
02:17:46,080 --> 02:17:52,080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: it led to a lot of changes in our budget delivery.

2245
02:17:52,160 --> 02:17:54,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It led to a lot of deliberations thanks to our former chairperson

2246
02:17:54,180 --> 02:17:57,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: who made it transparent, live-streamed, and the like.

2247
02:17:58,080 --> 02:18:03,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, somehow, we'd like to see the silver lining in all of what's happening.

2248
02:18:03,380 --> 02:18:08,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I'd like to think that partly, you know,

2249
02:18:08,720 --> 02:18:13,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: your higher conviction rates now may have been also influenced by

2250
02:18:13,900 --> 02:18:21,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: or, you know, brought about by the public's, you know, desire for accountability.

2251
02:18:22,160 --> 02:18:23,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

2252
02:18:23,160 --> 02:18:27,300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, we go to your structural integrity.

2253
02:18:27,300 --> 02:18:36,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You're only a kilometer away from the Marikina Valley fault line.

2254
02:18:36,440 --> 02:18:37,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What do you mean?

2255
02:18:37,440 --> 02:18:38,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is there...

2256
02:18:38,440 --> 02:18:44,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Do you need a budget apart from buying or purchasing or building, rather, a new building?

2257
02:18:44,720 --> 02:18:51,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is there an immediate intervention to check on the structural defects and correct it?

2258
02:18:51,180 --> 02:18:53,340
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: There were already studies conducted.

2259
02:18:53,340 --> 02:18:56,840
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: One by a private firm.

2260
02:18:57,400 --> 02:19:00,640
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: And this was confirmed by the DPWH as well.

2261
02:19:01,220 --> 02:19:04,380
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: And they confirmed that there are structural defects, indeed,

2262
02:19:04,520 --> 02:19:07,720
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: in our building that we are using right now.

2263
02:19:08,300 --> 02:19:16,780
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: But to repair this would also entail around 400 million, your honors.

2264
02:19:17,000 --> 02:19:22,380
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: But the problem is, if we repair this, we cannot stop hearing cases.

2265
02:19:22,580 --> 02:19:23,320
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Where we are now, we cannot stop hearing cases.

2266
02:19:23,320 --> 02:19:23,900
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Where will we go?

2267
02:19:24,920 --> 02:19:31,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And that's why you are appealing that the 500 million for the new building be...

2268
02:19:31,040 --> 02:19:31,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is that right?

2269
02:19:31,500 --> 02:19:31,700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is that right?

2270
02:19:31,860 --> 02:19:32,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 500 million?

2271
02:19:32,940 --> 02:19:43,580
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: So, we decided we will take the risk, continue occupying a building that is not structurally sound,

2272
02:19:44,460 --> 02:19:48,360
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: and instead opt to build a new building and transfer.

2273
02:19:48,360 --> 02:19:52,360
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Because we cannot stop the...

2274
02:19:52,360 --> 02:19:53,460
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Trial.

2275
02:19:53,460 --> 02:20:00,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But in the meantime, while the construction is ongoing, you remain structurally unsound

2276
02:20:00,940 --> 02:20:02,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: in a building that's structurally unsound.

2277
02:20:03,220 --> 02:20:03,660
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Yes, sir.

2278
02:20:05,160 --> 02:20:08,500
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Ourselves, our staff, and the court users.

2279
02:20:09,260 --> 02:20:09,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Exactly.

2280
02:20:12,260 --> 02:20:18,620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Well, in the JBC, the building that we are renting is structurally unsound.

2281
02:20:18,620 --> 02:20:21,620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It's being built.

2282
02:20:22,360 --> 02:20:31,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, what was recommended is we find another building to rent, right?

2283
02:20:31,300 --> 02:20:31,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We transfer.

2284
02:20:32,520 --> 02:20:37,240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's not part of your options to ensure your safety?

2285
02:20:38,460 --> 02:20:40,100
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Not for now, sir.

2286
02:20:40,200 --> 02:20:43,200
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: Rental will also incur additional expense.

2287
02:20:43,660 --> 02:20:46,740
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: And we need to fit out the rented space.

2288
02:20:47,140 --> 02:20:48,720
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: We also need to relocate.

2289
02:20:48,720 --> 02:20:51,720
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: And when we do, somehow or definitely...

2290
02:20:52,360 --> 02:20:57,020
Sandiganbayan Presiding Justice Geraldine Faith A. Econg: The processing of the cases will also be affected.

2291
02:20:58,020 --> 02:20:58,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yeah.

2292
02:20:58,540 --> 02:21:00,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But, of course, safety first, right?

2293
02:21:00,420 --> 02:21:00,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's what they said.

2294
02:21:01,300 --> 02:21:09,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, that's a concern that we in the legislative branch in the Senate would like to figure out how we can address.

2295
02:21:10,220 --> 02:21:18,500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Anyway, if there are, you know, moving forward, suggestions from the court administrator, if there are any,

2296
02:21:18,500 --> 02:21:22,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: because we want to make sure that you are safe.

2297
02:21:22,360 --> 02:21:28,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And if there are some stopgap measures, apart from the construction, I don't know.

2298
02:21:32,520 --> 02:21:35,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Justice Musking, you'd like to...

2299
02:21:37,930 --> 02:21:41,610
Sandiganbayan Associate Justice Michael Frederick L. Musngi: Thank you, Mr. Chair, Mr. Senate President.

2300
02:21:41,890 --> 02:21:49,950
Sandiganbayan Associate Justice Michael Frederick L. Musngi: I was just conferring with my colleagues that as a special court, we are conscious of our mandate and we do have special needs.

2301
02:21:49,950 --> 02:21:56,790
Sandiganbayan Associate Justice Michael Frederick L. Musngi: We'd be very happy to share our special needs through the Office of the Court Administrator.

2302
02:21:56,910 --> 02:22:02,310
Sandiganbayan Associate Justice Michael Frederick L. Musngi: For the reasons already discussed and explained in this August Chamber.

2303
02:22:02,650 --> 02:22:03,630
Sandiganbayan Associate Justice Michael Frederick L. Musngi: Thank you very much, Chair.

2304
02:22:03,730 --> 02:22:03,950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

2305
02:22:04,170 --> 02:22:04,430
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

2306
02:22:04,730 --> 02:22:16,230
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Anyway, our office is more than willing to look into this as we deliberate on the budget until its approval by December.

2307
02:22:16,970 --> 02:22:17,130
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sure.

2308
02:22:17,130 --> 02:22:19,490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: There are additional interventions that we may do.

2309
02:22:19,790 --> 02:22:20,490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Let us know, no?

2310
02:22:20,730 --> 02:22:21,070
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead.

2311
02:22:21,530 --> 02:22:22,950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, Senator J.V.

2312
02:22:23,730 --> 02:22:24,030
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Migs.

2313
02:22:24,350 --> 02:22:24,870
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you, Sherman.

2314
02:22:24,870 --> 02:22:25,870
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I just...

2315
02:22:26,910 --> 02:22:32,210
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Since the topic is on infrastructure, I just wanted to ask the members of the Court of Appeals here.

2316
02:22:34,210 --> 02:22:45,650
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I had initially put amount of 200, I'm not sure if it's 250 or 200 million to help the Northern Mindanao Court of Appeals

2317
02:22:45,650 --> 02:22:54,310
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: because our brothers, the justices of the Court of Appeals in Mindanao,

2318
02:22:54,310 --> 02:22:56,310
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and I know you're based in Cagayan de Oro.

2319
02:22:56,450 --> 02:22:56,890
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So what I...

2320
02:22:56,910 --> 02:23:01,650
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So what I initially did, being a proponent of Northern Mindanao, I'm from Northern Mindanao, Cagayan de Oro, Bukidnon,

2321
02:23:02,130 --> 02:23:05,170
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: we put a fund of about 200 million.

2322
02:23:06,530 --> 02:23:09,130
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: That was about a few years ago, maybe about five years ago.

2323
02:23:09,530 --> 02:23:14,710
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Any developments, Your Honor, on building them a decent building in the area?

2324
02:23:14,710 --> 02:23:22,070
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Because I can, again, make the institutional amendments for the Court of Appeals of Northern Mindanao,

2325
02:23:22,450 --> 02:23:26,550
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: being a proud citizen of that area.

2326
02:23:26,910 --> 02:23:35,910
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Your Honor, right now, they're renting, if I'm not mistaken, they're renting the building that is being used by the Court of Appeals.

2327
02:23:36,010 --> 02:23:38,590
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Any news on that or any developments on that, Your Honors?

2328
02:23:42,010 --> 02:23:43,070
Court of Appeals Presiding Justice Fernanda Lampas-Peralta: Thank you, Your Honor.

2329
02:23:44,570 --> 02:23:52,510
Court of Appeals Presiding Justice Fernanda Lampas-Peralta: May I just inform that in 2012, July 17, the Supreme Court issued a resolution

2330
02:23:53,370 --> 02:23:59,510
Court of Appeals Presiding Justice Fernanda Lampas-Peralta: approving the allocation from existing savings of the Supreme Court of certain...

2331
02:23:59,630 --> 02:24:08,550
Court of Appeals Presiding Justice Fernanda Lampas-Peralta: amounts for the construction of courthouses, which include Cagayan de Oro Court of Appeals building.

2332
02:24:08,550 --> 02:24:20,910
Court of Appeals Presiding Justice Fernanda Lampas-Peralta: And may I also inform that the Court of Appeals building is not included in the proposed augmentation in the present budget.

2333
02:24:23,810 --> 02:24:24,850
Court of Appeals Presiding Justice Fernanda Lampas-Peralta: Only Cebu.

2334
02:24:26,370 --> 02:24:27,790
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Your Honor, if...

2335
02:24:27,790 --> 02:24:28,670
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May I get the commitment?

2336
02:24:28,890 --> 02:24:29,550
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Because I already put...

2337
02:24:29,630 --> 02:24:30,250
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: funds there.

2338
02:24:30,670 --> 02:24:32,730
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And it goes to the general fund of the Judiciary.

2339
02:24:33,190 --> 02:24:36,530
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So, one way or the other, siguro nagamit yun for whatever reason.

2340
02:24:36,530 --> 02:24:41,890
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: If I make the institutional amendment through the chairman of the subcommittee,

2341
02:24:42,430 --> 02:24:50,370
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: may I get an assurance from the Judiciary that we can actually finally build them a building in the great city of Cagayan de Oro?

2342
02:24:51,290 --> 02:24:59,490
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I recall seeing many justices there recently when we took up the BARM initiatives of the Chief Justice.

2343
02:24:59,630 --> 02:25:04,030
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And it's a waste if we can't continue the area development.

2344
02:25:05,030 --> 02:25:09,430
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: But rest assured, this budget, I will make the institutional amendment necessary.

2345
02:25:09,430 --> 02:25:15,830
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Just let us know how much you need for the building for the Court of Appeals.

2346
02:25:22,680 --> 02:25:25,880
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Your Honor, Mr. Chairman, I also give budgets to...

2347
02:25:25,880 --> 02:25:28,660
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I have three courts in Bukidnon.

2348
02:25:29,440 --> 02:25:32,720
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Manolo Fortich, I think the court...

2349
02:25:32,720 --> 02:25:33,400
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: RTC courts.

2350
02:25:33,880 --> 02:25:35,680
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So, I've been giving RTC courts.

2351
02:25:35,800 --> 02:25:38,580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: In support to the Judiciary in the area.

2352
02:25:39,120 --> 02:25:42,280
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: But this is a big one because it's really the Court of Appeals.

2353
02:25:42,420 --> 02:25:45,120
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I believe the Court of Appeals is based in Cagayan de Oro.

2354
02:25:45,640 --> 02:25:47,920
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So, pride po namin yan, being from northern Mindanao.

2355
02:25:48,920 --> 02:25:50,280
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Wala po, they're just fending.

2356
02:25:50,440 --> 02:25:52,380
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: At minsan, tumutulo pa nga.

2357
02:25:52,620 --> 02:25:56,140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: At pag nagkaka-brown out, meron lang silang genset.

2358
02:25:56,220 --> 02:26:02,000
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So, I think best to modernize the Court of Appeals in Mindanao.

2359
02:26:02,000 --> 02:26:03,840
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And I'm willing, Mr. President.

2360
02:26:03,840 --> 02:26:07,960
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I'm willing to make that initiative for the Court of Appeals there.

2361
02:26:08,060 --> 02:26:08,560
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you, Your Honor.

2362
02:26:08,780 --> 02:26:10,160
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Justice Midas.

2363
02:26:10,500 --> 02:26:12,000
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2364
02:26:12,100 --> 02:26:15,560
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: Just in response to the query of Senator Subiri.

2365
02:26:17,400 --> 02:26:20,640
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: We have a judicial complex in Cagayan de Oro.

2366
02:26:20,900 --> 02:26:24,340
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: We're coming up with a judicial complex in Cagayan de Oro.

2367
02:26:24,680 --> 02:26:26,960
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: So, it's composed of two buildings.

2368
02:26:27,100 --> 02:26:30,160
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: One building for CACDO.

2369
02:26:30,160 --> 02:26:33,100
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: And the other building is for the lower courts.

2370
02:26:33,840 --> 02:26:41,400
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: At present, there's already, I think, a DAED for the lower courts.

2371
02:26:41,500 --> 02:26:49,020
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: So, we're just trying to match the designs for the two buildings.

2372
02:26:49,120 --> 02:26:52,240
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: For the CA and the first and second level courts.

2373
02:26:52,740 --> 02:26:56,520
Associate Justice Jose Midas P. Marquez: Rest assured, Your Honor, it's being done.

